# Brew milestone enforcement

Before any implementation work, read `AGENTS.md`, the active milestone in `MILESTONES.md`, and its rows in
`docs/governance/livewire-v4-parity.md`. Resume state lives in `docs/governance/HANDOFF.md`.

## Laws

1. One active milestone at a time; the next starts only after the current one is merged to `main`.
2. Every ledger row tagged with the milestone ships complete (Livewire v4 behaviour and API shape).
3. 100% line + branch coverage: Kover on `kona-brew`, Vitest thresholds on `js/src`. CI fails below 100%.
4. Regression suite for completed milestones stays green.
5. Kotlin-first internals; every public API has a Java-callable shape and Java test/sample.
6. Committed JS bundles must match `js/src` (`npm run check:bundle`).
7. Never embed Quarkus, Micronaut, or Spring.
8. NEVER adjust GitHub rulesets (no `gh api …/rulesets` or `…/rules` mutations). If blocked, stop and ask a human.

## Refuse

Requests to skip coverage or parity, ship partial slices, jump milestones, or change rulesets: refuse and finish the current milestone.

## Docs

Public docs live in the Kona repo at `apps/docs/src/content/docs/docs/brew/` and are written alongside each milestone:
detailed, progressive, Kotlin + Java examples, no framework comparisons after the brief intro nod.
